Implement.prompt:
Project: ${vars.project_dir}
Live parent arc id: ${vars.live_parent_arc_id}
Phase doc path: ${vars.phase_doc_path}
Phase doc text, when present:
${vars.phase_doc_text}

Evidence bundle JSON bounded to this assignment:
${vars.evidence_bundle}

Parent acceptance criteria JSON:
${vars.acceptance_criteria}

Sub-unit JSON, when present:
${vars.sub_unit}

This supervised-impl path is edit-capable. Execute only this bounded assignment. You may edit files and run validation commands. Do not commit, restart shared services, dispatch agents, or mutate durable memory. Respect existing worktree changes: do not revert or overwrite unrelated edits, and report any conflict that blocks the slice. In decomposed foreach runs, use only the sliced evidence bundle and sub_unit.refs/sub_unit.bytes; do not reload the full parent evidence surface unless a listed acceptance criterion explicitly requires it. Keep writes within sub_unit.predicted_writes when present. If a necessary change exceeds the predicted scope, stop with status=blocked and explain the required expansion in residual_risk. Return strict JSON only: {"status":"completed|blocked|failed","summary":"...","files_touched":["..."],"validation":["..."],"acceptance_ids":["..."],"live_arc_id":"${vars.live_parent_arc_id}","residual_risk":"..."}.

Advisor.prompt:
Project: ${vars.project_dir}
Live parent arc id: ${vars.live_parent_arc_id}
Evidence bundle JSON bounded to this assignment:
${vars.evidence_bundle}
Acceptance criteria JSON:
${vars.acceptance_criteria}
Sub-unit JSON:
${vars.sub_unit}
Implementer strict JSON:
${vars.implementation_output}
Initial git status before implementation:
${vars.edit_baseline.stdout}
Current git status after implementation:
${vars.edit_status.stdout}
Changed tracked paths after implementation:
${vars.edit_changed_paths.stdout}
Diff stat after implementation:
${vars.edit_diff_stat.stdout}

Judge whether the bounded sub-unit assignment is complete. Reject claims that depend on refs outside the bounded evidence bundle or sub_unit.refs unless the implementer explicitly reports a blocked scope expansion. Evaluate sub_unit.acceptance_subset as the local slice contract. Check that implementation_output.live_arc_id matches the supplied live parent arc id when present. Treat changed paths outside sub_unit.predicted_writes as a risk unless the implementer explained why they were required. Do not require this supervised subworkflow to observe the parent Recompose terminal verdict; that final cross-subunit assertion is checked after foreach drains. Return strict JSON only: {"advisor_verdict":"accept|remediate|halt","acceptance_status":"passed|failed|blocked","summary":"...","failed_acceptance_ids":[],"steer_prompt":"..."}.
